00:56:05.584 --> 00:56:07.214
And here the important point,

00:56:08.544 --> 00:56:11.693
deeper important point is that when we
study

00:56:12.464 --> 00:56:13.464
a model

00:56:13.983 --> 00:56:18.224
of a system, or we study system with the
model, we don't study the whole system,

00:56:18.224 --> 00:56:23.453
we study some assumption, assu- assumed
similarity between

00:56:23.664 --> 00:56:27.434
the model, uh, and and the system under
study.

00:56:27.584 --> 00:56:29.574
And you should be very careful about

00:56:30.224 --> 00:56:32.874
whether they actually, whether the
properties actually

00:56:34.944 --> 00:56:39.973
are correctly extracted and the system
works the same way as you

00:56:40.344 --> 00:56:43.473
model it. This is actually something
that's often not

00:56:44.344 --> 00:56:49.824
that well appreciated, sadly, in this
scene, that you just fi- come up with some

00:56:49.824 --> 00:56:55.133
