01:13:58.384 --> 01:14:03.584
the thermostat. So this is also
considerable deb- uh, subject of

01:14:03.584 --> 01:14:07.133
considerable debate in some corners of
philosophy.

01:14:08.064 --> 01:14:11.213
But the question is that, is a thermostat

01:14:12.184 --> 01:14:13.813
a cognitive system?

01:14:14.624 --> 01:14:19.734
Okay, so as I, my, my view, as I
established, is that, uh,

01:14:20.104 --> 01:14:25.184
it's not the thermostat that is cognitive
and not maybe even the

01:14:25.184 --> 01:14:30.474
perspective, uh, the behavior, but the
question is whether it makes sense

01:14:30.984 --> 01:14:36.073
to try to understand some behavior of the
thermostat, uh,

01:14:36.344 --> 01:14:37.453
use- using this

01:14:38.104 --> 01:14:40.493
information processing perspective.

01:14:42.744 --> 01:14:43.744
And, uh,

01:14:44.544 --> 01:14:49.474
thermostats are, well, they clearly have
this, you can, you can clearly

01:14:49.784 --> 01:14:51.974
draw this perception action loop.

01:14:52.384 --> 01:14:53.384
So you have,

01:14:53.824 --> 01:14:54.824
have the

01:14:55.624 --> 01:15:00.574
thermostat in some room, and then it makes
readings of the temperature.

01:15:01.224 --> 01:15:04.973
Uh, actually it can be just totally, uh,

01:15:07.064 --> 01:15:11.144
totally mechanical, so like metallic strip
expanding or contracting depending on

01:15:11.144 --> 01:15:12.174
the temperature.

01:15:13.344 --> 01:15:17.473
Uh, and then it it makes some sort of a

01:15:17.944 --> 01:15:19.174
computation.

01:15:20.104 --> 01:15:25.184
So here this would be P controller or uh
proportional controller we will

01:15:25.184 --> 01:15:26.653
encounter later as well.

01:15:27.544 --> 01:15:29.114
But here we can see that

01:15:29.864 --> 01:15:34.613
the thermostat is set to some target here,
T0.

01:15:35.024 --> 01:15:37.694
You can see it's here it's 20 degrees.

01:15:40.544 --> 01:15:46.174
And then it's has observed the temperature,
so it has perceived the temperature,

01:15:46.304 --> 01:15:51.894
and it computes their difference and tries
to move it towards the, uh,

01:15:52.144 --> 01:15:57.713
desired temperature. So exactly like you
could use in the, uh, out- uh,

01:15:58.464 --> 01:15:59.933
automated, uh,

01:16:01.784 --> 01:16:05.493
what was it? Well, in the, in the car that
follows the other car automatically.

01:16:07.904 --> 01:16:09.854
So it seems that, well,

01:16:10.704 --> 01:16:15.064
we have this computation, but importantly,
the computation doesn't necessarily

01:16:15.064 --> 01:16:20.153
happen as such. There's no computer in
this, uh, manual, uh,

01:16:21.784 --> 01:16:24.054
or these, uh, physical thermostats.

01:16:24.584 --> 01:16:29.173
But it does, uh, exhibit this property
that we can

01:16:29.384 --> 01:16:34.384
approximate it using some sort of equation
that you can turn into a

01:16:34.384 --> 01:16:35.384
computation.

01:16:36.064 --> 01:16:38.173
And it has a goal.

01:16:39.344 --> 01:16:44.074
It's some sense seems to adapt, uh, to
each

01:16:44.304 --> 01:16:49.234
environment. So if the temperature, uh,
increases, it,

01:16:49.904 --> 01:16:50.904
uh,

01:16:51.184 --> 01:16:53.263
cools down if it's too high and so on.

01:16:53.263 --> 01:16:57.174
So there is some variation and, uh,

01:16:58.224 --> 01:17:02.624
partially predictable, uh, changes in the
environment.

01:17:02.624 --> 01:17:04.454
So we know from the, we

01:17:05.304 --> 01:17:08.574
know that we, or we can assume that the,
uh,

01:17:10.224 --> 01:17:14.584
that the temperature doesn't just spike up
immediately to 1000 degrees Celsius.

01:17:14.584 --> 01:17:19.813
So we can know something about, uh, how
the temperature will behave.

01:17:19.824 --> 01:17:23.334
Of course, we cannot fully behave, fully,
uh,

01:17:24.224 --> 01:17:25.934
predict it, uh,

01:17:26.664 --> 01:17:30.424
with then, because then we have to do this
approximate weather forecast in a

01:17:30.424 --> 01:17:35.664
very complex system, so it's only we can
predict some statistical, uh,

01:17:35.664 --> 01:17:39.893
behavior of how it will, uh, operate in
the future.

01:17:41.824 --> 01:17:46.104
Uh, there's the complexity, but that, of
course, that is clearly simpler system

01:17:46.104 --> 01:17:49.854
than the room itself and all the air and
stuff in it.

01:17:51.304 --> 01:17:52.304
Uh,

01:17:53.504 --> 01:17:54.533
so sort of from

01:17:55.224 --> 01:17:58.294
this perspective, it does seem to fit,

01:17:59.224 --> 01:18:00.253
uh, all,

01:18:02.464 --> 01:18:03.954
fit all the, uh,

01:18:04.584 --> 01:18:06.713
criteria for our intelligent

01:18:07.784 --> 01:18:08.784
behavior.

01:18:09.784 --> 01:18:15.264
So if you use that criteria and accept
that this fulfills that, those criteria,

01:18:15.264 --> 01:18:16.264
then you would

01:18:16.584 --> 01:18:21.214
logically have to admit that it does
intelligent behavior in this sense.

01:18:23.064 --> 01:18:24.734
Okay, so have I managed to

01:18:25.744 --> 01:18:31.053
convince anybody now that the thermostat
is actually a cognitive system?

01:18:32.544 --> 01:18:33.544
Hands up.

