Okay, but we will close up with another

01:18:49.904 --> 01:18:51.833
excerpt from the same paper.

01:18:51.984 --> 01:18:52.984
Actually, this is

01:18:53.464 --> 01:18:55.893
Even the same paragraph, it continues

01:18:56.544 --> 01:18:58.173
exactly from the previous one.

01:18:59.424 --> 01:19:04.913
So there Turing writes, if we are able to
explain and predict

01:19:05.584 --> 01:19:10.944
the behavior of something, or there seems
to be little underlying plan, we

01:19:10.944 --> 01:19:14.313
have little temptation to imagine

01:19:15.184 --> 01:19:16.184
intelligence.

01:19:16.904 --> 01:19:21.584
With the same object, therefore, it is
possible that one man would consider it

01:19:21.584 --> 01:19:24.533
as intelligent and another would not.

01:19:26.104 --> 01:19:27.104
And

01:19:27.544 --> 01:19:28.544
the other

01:19:29.424 --> 01:19:31.334
would have not, uh,

01:19:32.904 --> 01:19:38.503
the other would deem it intelligent
because they have not found out the

01:19:38.503 --> 01:19:40.333
rules of its behavior.

01:19:42.064 --> 01:19:43.064
So they,

01:19:43.944 --> 01:19:46.173
in a sense, if some, if the

01:19:46.944 --> 01:19:52.344
guy hasn't, the guy, guy doesn't understand
the system, it doesn't understand

01:19:52.344 --> 01:19:57.674
the information processing, the rules of
behavior of the system, so it

01:19:57.704 --> 01:20:03.174
thinks, so then they think, uh, that the
system is intelligent.

01:20:05.304 --> 01:20:10.194
And here we come the thermostat idea that
maybe why you don't deem that

01:20:10.224 --> 01:20:15.624
thermostat is, uh, intelligent is that you
think you understand

01:20:15.624 --> 01:20:17.424
how it works, somehow simple.

01:20:17.424 --> 01:20:22.494
It's rules of behavior are something that
you can grasp quite easily, and then

01:20:22.864 --> 01:20:28.424
you don't have to sort of apply this
perspective of in- intelligence.

01:20:28.424 --> 01:20:33.904
You don't, it's not useful to think of it,
uh, analogously to other things

01:20:33.904 --> 01:20:37.733
that you think are intelligent, like
humans or animals, which have very

01:20:38.184 --> 01:20:39.733
complicated behavior, which

01:20:40.864 --> 01:20:41.864
are better,

01:20:42.504 --> 01:20:44.774
better analyzed somehow else.

01:20:47.544 --> 01:20:48.544
uh,

01:20:50.624 --> 01:20:53.454
but sort of here, this relates to

01:20:54.224 --> 01:20:59.504
many of the old sayings in machine
learning, or the AI, as it was

01:20:59.504 --> 01:21:03.973
called, uh, before it was called machine
learning, and then it was called AI

01:21:03.983 --> 01:21:09.174
again. It's another historical thing, but
there was this common

01:21:09.224 --> 01:21:14.254
wisdom that when something, when you have
a system that does seem to do some,

01:21:14.504 --> 01:21:17.914
computer system that seems to do
something, uh,

01:21:18.544 --> 01:21:23.414
complicated, the behavior is somehow hard
to figure out, then people will think,

01:21:23.424 --> 01:21:28.414
okay, that, that system may be
intelligent, but once you

01:21:28.544 --> 01:21:33.904
understand how it ticks inside, once you
understand its rules of behavior, now

01:21:33.904 --> 01:21:36.234
you suddenly think that, okay, it's,

01:21:36.904 --> 01:21:39.024
it, it's not an intelligent system.

01:21:39.024 --> 01:21:44.433
So once, once AI becomes understood, it
stops being, uh,

01:21:44.704 --> 01:21:45.704
intelligence.

01:21:48.864 --> 01:21:50.193
Maybe I will try here

01:21:50.944 --> 01:21:56.074
to sort of flip this out to make you think
